# ABP Modularity

## Module Class
```csharp
[DependsOn(
    typeof(AbpDddDomainModule),
    typeof(AbpEntityFrameworkCoreModule)
)]
public class BookStoreApplicationModule : AbpModule
{
    public override void PreConfigureServices(ServiceConfigurationContext context)
    {
        // Pre-configuration (before other modules)
    }

    public override void ConfigureServices(ServiceConfigurationContext context)
    {
        // Service registration and configuration
        Configure<AbpAutoMapperOptions>(options =>
        {
            options.AddMaps<BookStoreApplicationModule>();
        });
    }

    public override void OnApplicationInitialization(ApplicationInitializationContext context)
    {
        // Application startup logic
        var app = context.GetApplicationBuilder();
        app.UseRouting();
    }
}
```

## Module Layering
```
MyModule.Domain.Shared    → Constants, enums, shared types
MyModule.Domain           → Entities, repository interfaces, domain services
MyModule.Application.Contracts → App service interfaces, DTOs
MyModule.Application      → App service implementations
MyModule.EntityFrameworkCore → EF Core DbContext, repository implementations
MyModule.HttpApi          → REST controllers (depends on Application.Contracts only)
MyModule.HttpApi.Client   → Remote client proxies
MyModule.Web              → UI (depends on HttpApi only)
```

## Dependency Direction
```
Web → HttpApi → Application.Contracts
Application → Domain + Application.Contracts
Domain → Domain.Shared
EF Core → Domain
```

## Best Practices
- Use `[DependsOn]` for explicit module dependencies
- Each module must be usable standalone
- Don't leak web concerns into domain/application
- Every package has exactly one `AbpModule` class
